      <floats-group id="article-27269.s15">
        <fig id="article-27269.image.f1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Suppurative Inguinal Lymphadenopathy (Bubo) Secondary to <italic toggle="yes">Yersinia pestis</italic> Infection. Hallmark inguinal bubo in a patient with bubonic plague, characterized by focal, painful lymph node enlargement that has progressed to spontaneous rupture and suppuration. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention&#x000a0;</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="1280px-Plague_-buboes" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-27269.s16">
        <fig id="article-27269.image.f2" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Gram Stain of <italic toggle="yes">Yersinia enterocolitica.</italic> Characteristic gram-negative coccobacillary appearance of <italic toggle="yes">Yersinia</italic> species, demonstrating the distinctive bipolar staining pattern that yields a classic safety pin morphology. Contributed by&#x000a0;O Chaigasame, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="yersinia" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-27269.s17">
        <fig id="article-27269.image.f3" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Zoonotic Transmission Cycle of <italic toggle="yes">Yersinia pestis.</italic> The transmission of Yersinia pestis from its primary rodent reservoir to accidental human hosts via the bite of an infected flea vector, such as <italic toggle="yes">Xenopsylla cheopis.</italic> Contributed by&#x000a0;S Bhimji, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Plague1" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
